-- a public page made once for each state of the source (the view's stamp) and kept in the store as the
-- response's bytes (STORE/site-STAMP-KEY), so a reader is served bytes and the machine renders nothing
-- (Avik, 2026-11-18: "its mission critical this never goes down again"); the child at start makes every
-- published page this way, one after another, before any reader asks; only a page that was answered (200)
-- is kept
s-site-or : List Word → Proc W (List Word) → Sum Unit (List Word) → Proc W (List Word)
s-site-or f mk (inr r) = ret {lzero} {W} r
s-site-or f mk (inl u) = bind mk (λ r → if h-prefix "HTTP/1.1 200" r then bind (h-write f r) (λ ok → ret {lzero} {W} r) else ret {lzero} {W} r)
